Quick PostgreSQL Verification

Run this command:

Shell
python -c "from chroma_db_code.db_tools import get_customer; print(get_customer('1001'))"

Expected:

Plain Text
('Ravi', 760, 50000, 'Home Loan')

If you get:

Plain Text
OperationalError

then PostgreSQL connection details are wrong.

If you get:

Plain Text
None

then customer 1001 does not exist.

Verify Database Data

Run:

Shell
sudo -u postgres psql loandb

Then:

SQL
SELECT * FROM customers;

Expected:

Plain Text
1001 | Ravi | 760 | 50000 | Home Loan
1002 | Amit | 680 | 30000 | Personal Loan
1003 | Priya | 810 | 75000 | Car Loan

Exit:

SQL
\q
Most Common Cause

In db_tools.py you probably have:

Python
conn = psycopg2.connect(
host="localhost",
database="loandb",
user="postgres",
password="postgres"
)

If the PostgreSQL user password isn't actually "postgres", you'll get:

Plain Text
psycopg2.OperationalError:
password authentication failed
Run These Two Commands
Shell
python -c "from chroma_db_code.db_tools import get_customer; print(get_customer('1001'))"

and

Shell
sudo -u postgres psql loandb -c "SELECT * FROM customers;"
